      "message": "As an aside: What does it even mean to apply ordering constraints to uniform memory? Is this assuming a world where uniforms can somehow be written to via aliasing another buffer?\n\nIt seems like Metal\u0027s uniform isn\u0027t actually an address space, it\u0027s just a type that uses the compiler to enforce uniformity (while the values are probably still in some other address space?)",
